# 227: overshooting the limit by fifty times over lands the SAME error at the
# same line — a limit, not a function of how far past it you asked to go. Only
# 1000 invocations ever happen, so this case is no slower than 226.
# It also asserts §3's "a program that fails at line 9 has the output of lines
# 1..8 and then the error": both printed lines survive ahead of the failure, so
# an engine that buffered output and dropped it on error diverges here.
--- source
print "start";
print 1 + 1;
fn deep(n) {
  if n == 0 { return 0; }
  return deep(n - 1);
}
print deep(50000);
--- expect
start
2
error: Value at line 5: recursion limit of 1000 frames exceeded
